{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"434c92b1abf6288e","type":"text","text":"# nslookup","x":1482,"y":877,"width":138,"height":60},
		{"id":"50480fd2409e0e2d","type":"text","text":"Nslookup is a command line tool used for querying the `DNS` domain name server to obtain `domain name` or `ip address` mapping information.","x":1740,"y":864,"width":540,"height":86},
		{"id":"b62f926cb68cc72f","type":"text","text":"This tool can help you `troubleshoot network connectivity` problems by checking `DNS configuration` and resolving `host names.`","x":1740,"y":1000,"width":540,"height":80},
		{"id":"974cccbc7ca3e6c5","type":"text","text":"`nslookup-type` : This command queries the `dns server` to return a specfic `DNS RECORD TYPE` for the give `domain name`.","x":2020,"y":1180,"width":270,"height":140},
		{"id":"1b0425b75ec9ae79","type":"text","text":"This command query the `DNS SERVER` to resolve the `IP ADDRESS` of the given `domain name` .","x":1740,"y":1180,"width":270,"height":140},
		{"id":"b4aa2ea1758e676f","type":"text","text":"nslookup [-option] [name | -] [server]","x":1740,"y":1440,"width":550,"height":60},
		{"id":"ba912b3e758184a7","type":"text","text":"# Examples","x":1937,"y":1660,"width":156,"height":60},
		{"id":"2fa1483cd1f7af41","type":"text","text":"### Basic Syntax\n`nslookup example.com 8.8.8.8                  :`  Look up a domain using the default resolve\n`nslookup -type=mx example.com             :`  Query a specific record type\n`nslookup 192.168.43.2                                : ` Run a reverse dns lookup\n`nslookup                                                      :`  Active intractive mode\n`nslookup localhost :` verify local name resolution\n`nslookup 127.0.0.1 : ` verify for loopback resolution\n`nslookup 192.168.2.2 : ` Reverse loopback for public ip address","x":2360,"y":1440,"width":650,"height":245},
		{"id":"821a9c8f657cc46e","type":"text","text":"### Specific dns server : compare answer with diffrent resolver\n`nslookup example.com 8.8.8.8` Query Google Public DNS\n`nslookup example.com 1.1.1.1 `Query Cloudflare DNS\n`nslookup example.com 9.9.9.9` Query Quad9\n`nslookup -type=mx example.com 8.8.8.8` Query MX records from a specific resolver\n`nslookup -type=txt example.com 1.1.1.1` Compare TXT answers between resolvers","x":1060,"y":1540,"width":660,"height":200},
		{"id":"73294a34ffe67d32","type":"text","text":"### Record Type : Use `-type` to query specific dns records\nUse `-type` to query specific DNS records.\n`nslookup -type=a example.com` Query IPv4 address records\n`nslookup -type=aaaa example.com` Query IPv6 address records\n`nslookup -type=mx example.com` Query mail exchanger records\n`nslookup -type=ns example.com` Query authoritative name servers\n`nslookup -type=txt example.com` Query TXT records\n`nslookup -type=soa example.com `Query the SOA (start of authority) record\n`nslookup -type=cname www.example.com` Check whether a hostname is an alias\n`nslookup -type=any example.com `Run an ANY query","x":2360,"y":1720,"width":650,"height":290},
		{"id":"33e37cd0a45b7955","type":"text","text":"### Interactive mode : Run multiple qry in a session\nInteractive Mode\nRun multiple queries in one session.\n`nslookup` Open interactive mode\n`set type=mx `Switch the active query type to MX\n`set type=txt `Switch the active query type to TXT\n`server 8.8.8.8 `Change the active DNS server\n`example.com` Query a domain after entering interactive mode\n`exit` Leave the interactive session","x":1060,"y":1780,"width":520,"height":260},
		{"id":"51953e91433903da","type":"text","text":"### Troubleshooting\nQuick checks for `common nslookup errors`.\n\n`NXDOMAIN` Verify the domain name and make sure it exists\n`SERVFAIL` Try another resolver such as 8.8.8.8 or 1.1.1.1\nConnection timed out; no servers could be\nreached Check network access and verify `/etc/resolv.conf`\nNon-authoritative answer Normal cached response from a resolver\nNo answer The queried record type is not set for that name","x":1060,"y":2080,"width":520,"height":300},
		{"id":"4201d221da459a46","x":1920,"y":1800,"width":292,"height":257,"type":"text","text":"|Type|Meaning|\n|---|---|\n|A|IPv4 Address|\n|AAAA|IPv6 Address|\n|MX|Mail Server|\n|NS|Name Server|\n|TXT|Text/SPF/Verification|\n|CNAME|Alias|\n|SOA|Start of Authority|"},
		{"id":"96c515589b66cd37","type":"text","text":"when no arguments are given (the default name server is used);","x":-320,"y":1229,"width":280,"height":80},
		{"id":"e765fd51fa422478","type":"text","text":"when the first argument is a `hyphen (-) ` and the second argument is the` host name` or internet address of a name server.\n","x":-320,"y":1347,"width":385,"height":107},
		{"id":"512d666e747f4217","type":"text","text":"# nslookup","x":-167,"y":914,"width":147,"height":60},
		{"id":"53b8c378960cff0e","type":"text","text":"Interactive mode allows the user to query name servers  for\n     information  about  various  hosts  and  domains  or to print a list of hosts in a domain.","x":200,"y":1240,"width":280,"height":160},
		{"id":"e9997c16b8670239","type":"text","text":"nslookup  is a program to query Internet domain name servers.  nslookup has two modes: in‐","x":215,"y":914,"width":626,"height":60},
		{"id":"1e49696cc9e7eec8","type":"text","text":"Interactive","x":215,"y":1090,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2cba078ed704d0e0","type":"text","text":"Non-Interactive","x":591,"y":1090,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1746801717917ccb","type":"text","text":"Non-interactive mode prints just the name and requested information for a host or domain.","x":591,"y":1240,"width":250,"height":160}
	],
